 "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:16:18Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "last question", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:16:20Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "10.\tX is the largest of all the upanishads, and it has a suitably grand name. Alongside the ChAndOgya, it is considered the oldest of the upanishads. Its most prominent sage is Y, one of the towering figures of Indian philosophy. In one of the upanishad's most moving passages, Y prepares to renounce the world and enter the life of a wandering ascetic. He calls his two wives, kAtyAyanI and maitrEyI, to divide his property between them. maitrEyI famously asks: \"If the entire earth, full of wealth, were mine, would I thereby become immortal?\" Y replies: \"No, your life would be like that of the wealthy — but there is no hope of immortality through wealth.\" maitrEyI then says: \"What should I do with that which will not make me immortal? Teach me instead what you know.\" This leads to Y’s discourse on the nature of the Atman. This upanishad is the source of the famous prayer that opens many Hindu ceremonies: \"asatO mA sadgamaya, tamasO mA jyOtirgamaya, mRtyOrmA amRtam gamaya\" — lead me from the unreal to the real, from darkness to light, from death to immortality. ID X (10 points) and Y (10 points).", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:16:54Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Brihandaryanka", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:16:55Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Brihadaranyaka", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:16:56Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Something", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:02Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Yajnavalkya", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:04Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "I have butchered the spelling", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:05Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Brihad*", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:16Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Great Forest Upanishad", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:22Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Has a lot of weird nonsense tbf", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:31Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Correct. Brihadaranyaka", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:32Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "I like the katha upanishad the most", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T04:17:54Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "This statement is so Akshay", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]